OL,3,GNEWSAHotels need 'minimum standards' to
OL,4,Akeep women safe
OL,5,
OL,6,FHotels should face national minimum
OL,7,Fstandards to protect female guests,
OL,8,Fwitnesses have told a parliamentary
OL,9,Fcommittee examining safety in the
OL,10,Findustry.
OL,12,FThe hearing followed an independent
OL,13,Freview into security failings at
OL,14,FTravelodge after a woman was sexually
OL,15,Fassaulted at one of its hotels in
OL,16,FMaidenhead, Berkshire.
OL,23,APub: 25-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB S Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
FL,332,330,200,160,0,100
PN,33102
SC,0002
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F331A1795640132
OL,1,W5j 5Qws js17kjc15 js57kj#4
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q,. *,$%**,%-,* %%**,! ,,,,,,
OL,3,GNEWSAHotels need 'minimum standards' to
OL,4,Akeep women safe
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe review's author, Paul Greaney KC,
OL,7,Fsaid room intrusions had become so
OL,8,Fcommon they were treated as something
OL,9,Fto be tolerated, while Travelodge's
OL,10,Finterim chief executive admitted the
OL,11,Fcompany had not taken guest safety
OL,12,Fseriously enough.
OL,14,FCommittee chair and Labour MP Olivia
OL,15,FBailey said the evidence showed not
OL,16,Fenough was being done to protect women
OL,17,Fand called for "concrete action".
OL,23,APub: 25-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG2/2
